{
 "events": [
  {
   "text": "Sergey Olegovich Sirotkin was born in Moscow, Russia.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "27 August 1995",
   "date": "1995-08-27",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "He graduated from Moscow Automobile and Road Construction University with a degree in race car engineering.",
   "chunk": 0,
   "date_text": "2017",
   "date": "2017",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 0,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#0"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin began karting.",
   "chunk": 1,
   "date_text": "2008",
   "date": "2008",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#1"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin progressed through to the KF3 and KF2 category.",
   "chunk": 1,
   "date_text": "2010",
   "date": "2010",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 1,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#1"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin graduated to single-seaters, racing in the newly launched Formula Abarth series in Italy for Jenzer Motorsport.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin made his début at Vallelunga.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished 18th in the championship.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin remained in Formula Abarth with Jenzer for a second season in 2011.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": "2011",
   "date": "2011",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Prior to the round at Spa, Sirotkin switched to the Euronova Racing by Fortec team.",
   "chunk": 2,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin won the European Series title with a race to spare.",
   "chunk": 3,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#3"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished as runner-up in the Italian Series.",
   "chunk": 3,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#3"
  },
  {
   "text": "In 2012, Sirotkin continued his collaboration with Euronova Racing into the Auto GP World Series.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": "2012",
   "date": "2012",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin scored his first win at Valencia, becoming the youngest Auto GP winner.",
   "chunk": 4,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#4"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished the season in third place overall.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin recorded his first pole position at the Marrakech Street Circuit.",
   "chunk": 5,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 2,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#5"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin participated in the Italian Formula Three Championship, driving for Euronova.",
   "chunk": 6,
   "date_text": "2012",
   "date": "2012",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#6"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin recorded two wins at the Hungaroring and Monza.",
   "chunk": 6,
   "date_text": "2012",
   "date": "2012",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#6"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished the season fifth overall in both the European and Italian Series championships.",
   "chunk": 6,
   "date_text": "2012",
   "date": "2012",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#6"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin made his Formula Renault 3.5 debut in his home event at the Moscow Raceway.",
   "chunk": 7,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#7"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin expanded his Formula Renault 3.5 campaign to contest a full season, competing with ISR Racing.",
   "chunk": 8,
   "date_text": "2013",
   "date": "2013",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#8"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin achieved the ninth place in the championship standings.",
   "chunk": 8,
   "date_text": "2013",
   "date": "2013",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#8"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin switched to the Fortec Motorsport team and partnered there with Oliver Rowland.",
   "chunk": 9,
   "date_text": "2014",
   "date": "2014",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#9"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin scored his first pole position and won his first Formula Renault 3.5 Series race on his home soil at Moscow Raceway.",
   "chunk": 9,
   "date_text": "2014",
   "date": "2014",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#9"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished 5th in the championship, with 132 points.",
   "chunk": 9,
   "date_text": "2014",
   "date": "2014",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 3,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#9"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was announced that Sirotkin would debut in the series with Rapax.",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": "February 2015",
   "date": "2015-02",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin won the feature race at Silverstone.",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished third in the overall standings.",
   "chunk": 10,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#10"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin switched to defending champions ART Grand Prix.",
   "chunk": 11,
   "date_text": "the 2016 season",
   "date": "2016",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin spun and stalled in the season opener at Barcelona.",
   "chunk": 11,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin crashed into the wall in the Feature race in Monaco.",
   "chunk": 11,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin took a double podium finish in both Feature and Sprint races in Baku.",
   "chunk": 11,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin took a pole position at Spielberg.",
   "chunk": 11,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin had another double podium finish in the Hungaroring round.",
   "chunk": 12,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin repeated success in the feature Hockenheim race.",
   "chunk": 12,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished second in Sepang.",
   "chunk": 12,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished third in the final race of the season at Abu Dhabi.",
   "chunk": 12,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin was classified third in the standings.",
   "chunk": 12,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin had a one-round return to the wheel of the Dallara GP2/11 car in the 2017 FIA Formula 2 Championship at Baku.",
   "chunk": 13,
   "date_text": "2017",
   "date": "2017",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#13"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin replaced injured Alexander Albon in ART Grand Prix.",
   "chunk": 13,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#13"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin finished both races of the round in points.",
   "chunk": 13,
   "date_text": null,
   "date": null,
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#13"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin returned to Formula 2 with ART Grand Prix for pre-season testing as a replacement for the quarantined Christian Lundgaard.",
   "chunk": 13,
   "date_text": "In 2020",
   "date": "2020",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 4,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#13"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin joined the Sauber Formula One team.",
   "chunk": 14,
   "date_text": "July 2013",
   "date": "2013-07",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#14"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin stayed in his role as test driver.",
   "chunk": 14,
   "date_text": "2014",
   "date": "2014",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#14"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin participated in tests that took place in Bahrain on 8 April.",
   "chunk": 14,
   "date_text": "8 April",
   "date": "2014-04-08",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#14"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin made his race weekend debut in free practice at the 2014 Russian Grand Prix.",
   "chunk": 14,
   "date_text": "2014",
   "date": "2014",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#14"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin was unable to secure a contract with Sauber for 2015.",
   "chunk": 15,
   "date_text": "2015",
   "date": "2015",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#15"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin's Formula One chances were revived when it was announced that he would act as a development driver for the Renault Sport F1 Team.",
   "chunk": 16,
   "date_text": "April 2016",
   "date": "2016-04",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#16"
  },
  {
   "text": "He became a reserve driver, remaining with Renault.",
   "chunk": 16,
   "date_text": "2017",
   "date": "2017",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#16"
  },
  {
   "text": "After the 2017 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix Sirotkin had a half-day test with Williams at the Yas Marina Circuit.",
   "chunk": 17,
   "date_text": "2017",
   "date": "2017",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#17"
  },
  {
   "text": "He was announced by Williams as their new driver for the season as the teammate of Lance Stroll.",
   "chunk": 17,
   "date_text": "January 2018",
   "date": "2018-01",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#17"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was announced that Sirotkin would not continue to race with Williams in 2019.",
   "chunk": 27,
   "date_text": "2019",
   "date": "2019",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#27"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin served as reserve driver for the Formula One teams of both McLaren and Renault.",
   "chunk": 28,
   "date_text": "In 2019",
   "date": "2019",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#28"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin continued as reserve driver for Renault.",
   "chunk": 28,
   "date_text": "in 2020",
   "date": "2020",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 5,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#28"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin raced at the 24 Hours of Le Mans for SMP Racing with Mikhail Aleshin and Viktor Shaytar.",
   "chunk": 29,
   "date_text": "2017",
   "date": "2017",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 6,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#29"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin drove a LMP1-class BR1 together with Stéphane Sarrazin and Egor Orudzhev.",
   "chunk": 29,
   "date_text": "2019",
   "date": "2019",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 6,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#29"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sirotkin signed with AF Corse to drive a factory-supported Ferrari 488 GT3 at the GT World Challenge Europe Endurance Cup.",
   "chunk": 29,
   "date_text": "2020",
   "date": "2020",
   "approximate": false,
   "section": 6,
   "flags": [],
   "cid": "/wiki/Sergey_Sirotkin_(racing_driver)#29"
  }
